# Build context for deploy/license-server/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<Dockerfile name>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile in
# preference to a root .dockerignore, so this applies only to the licence
# server image.
#
# Allow-list: everything is excluded, then exactly what the build reads is let
# back in. The point is less the size of the context than what is NOT in it —
# the signing key, .env files and release artefacts never reach the builder,
# so they cannot end up in a layer by accident.

*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.npmrc
!tsconfig*.json
!server.vite.config.ts
!src/shared/**
!src/server/**
!src/main/database/sqlite.ts

# Belt and braces: never, even if a rule above is widened later.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.env
**/.env.*
